==Dutch==

===Etymology===
{{bor+|nl|en|prairie}}, from {{der|nl|fr|prairie}}, from {{der|nl|frm|prairie}}, from {{der|nl|fro|praerie}}, from {{der|nl|la|pratum}}. Re-borrowed from English after {{noncog|dum|praierie}} (also from {{noncog|frm|prairie}}) fell out of use. Related to {{m|nl|prieel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈprɛː.ri/|/ˈprɛ.ri/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-prairie.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|prai|rie}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|f|-s|-}}

# {{l|en|prairie}} {{defdate|from ca. 1830s}}
#* '''1831''', James Fenimore Cooper, ''De prairie, of Grazige woestijn van Noord-Amerika'', vol. 1, tr. from English, A. & J. Honkoop (publ.), page 339.
#*: {{quote|nl|De slangen der '''Prairie''' zijn niet vergiftig, uitgezonderd eenige vergramde ratelslangen, welker ratel hen intusschen steeds aanmeldt, voor dat zij u eenig kwaad doen.|The snakes of the '''prairie''' are not venomous, some angered rattlesnakes excepted, whose rattle in the meantime announces them each time, before they do any harm to you.}}

